 parms←∆StormGuardParms(name entries);folder
⍝ Returns HandleError's parameters as Plodder's `SetErrorParms` establishes them from an INI file
⍝ whose [TRAP] section holds `entries`, a vector of lines such as 'StormCeiling = 2'.
⍝ The error folder is `<test folder>/<name>/Errors`, a fresh one for every test case, so the
⍝ storm guard always starts without any history.
⍝ The parameters are then made light-weight: no component file, no custom function, no log function
⍝ (Plodder itself already does without an error WS). The HTML report remains: it tells which
⍝ crashes got the full treatment.
⍝ Instead of `⎕OFF`, `Process` signals 689, as it does in a server; `∆ProvokeCrash` catches that.
 folder←∆GetTestFolder,'/',name
 ##.Plodder.⎕SHADOW'G'                              ⍝ Both are locals of `Run` in a running server,
 ##.Plodder.⎕SHADOW'F'                              ⍝ so they must be established here
 ##.Plodder.G←⎕NS''
 ##.Plodder.G.INI←∆CreateIni name((⊂'[TRAP]'),(⊂'Folder = ''',folder,'/Errors'''),entries)
 ##.Plodder.F←##.FilesAndDirs
 parms←##.Plodder.SetErrorParms ##.HandleError.CreateParms
 parms.saveCrash←0
 parms.saveVars←0
 parms.customFns←''
 parms.logFunction←''
 parms.off←0
 parms.signal←689
⍝Done
